.TH GLIMPSE 1 2026-10-27 glimpse "User Commands"
.SH NAME
glimpse \- a terminal pager for huge files and endless streams
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B glimpse
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ FILE | \- ]
.br
.IB command " | glimpse"
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B glimpse
shows a file, or its standard input, one screen at a time.
It stays responsive on very large files and on indefinitely long lines,
renders ANSI colors and man-page overstrikes safely, and never passes
terminal control sequences from the input through to the terminal.
.PP
Regular files are read in place and watched for appends, truncation, and
(with
.BR \-\-follow\-name )
replacement.
Pipes are buffered in memory up to
.B \-\-memory\-budget
and then in a private temporary spool file up to
.BR \-\-spool\-quota .
.PP
When standard output is not a terminal,
.B glimpse
copies its input unchanged, like
.BR cat (1).
Keyboard input is read from the controlling terminal, so piped input works.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Viewing
.TP
.B \-\-follow
Keep the view at the end of the input as it grows (toggle with
.BR F ).
.TP
.B \-\-follow\-name
Watch a file by its path, like
.BR "tail \-F" :
reopen it when the path names a different file after rotation, and wait while
it is missing.
By default the open file is followed, like
.BR "tail \-f" .
.TP
.BI \-j " N" "\fR, \fP\-\-jump\-target=" N
Screen line where search matches and line jumps land:
.B 1
is the top,
.B \-1
the bottom, and a value with a decimal point such as
.B .5
a fraction of the screen height.
.TP
.BR \-N ", " \-\-line\-numbers
Show a line number gutter (toggle with
.BR # ).
.TP
.B \-\-hex\-colors
Color each
.BI # RRGGBB
code with the color it names (toggle with
.BR R ).
Codes must stand alone, not inside a longer word or number.
It needs a truecolor terminal, detected from
.B COLORTERM
or a
.B \-direct
or
.B \-truecolor
.BR TERM ;
otherwise nothing is colored.
.TP
.BR \-\-wrap =\fIbool\fP
Wrap long lines (the default).
With
.BR \-\-wrap=false ,
each line is one row and
.BR h / l
scroll horizontally.
.TP
.BI \-\-cmdheight " N"
Footer layout:
.B 0
(default) statusline with a prompt row added on demand;
.B 1
permanent statusline and prompt rows;
.B \-1
one shared row that
.B =
toggles;
.B \-2
like \-1 with the statusline initially hidden.
.TP
.BI \-\-label " NAME"
Name shown for the input in the statusline.
Standard input defaults to
.BR $MAN_PN ,
which
.BR man (1)
sets to the page name.
.TP
.BI \-\-ambiguous\-width " N"
Width of East Asian ambiguous characters: 1 or 2 cells.
.SS Searching
.TP
.B \-\-smart\-case
Ignore case unless the query contains an uppercase letter.
.TP
.B \-\-ignore\-case
Always ignore case.
.TP
.B \-\-case\-sensitive
Match case exactly.
.TP
.B \-\-incremental\-search
Preview matches while typing a search.
.TP
.BR \-\-highlight\-search =\fIbool\fP
Highlight visible matches (default true).
.SS Storage
.TP
.BI \-\-memory\-budget " BYTES"
Input bytes kept in memory before spooling (default 64 MiB).
.TP
.BI \-\-spool\-quota " BYTES"
Maximum spooled stream size; reading pauses when it is full until
.B :set spool\-quota=
raises it (default 1 GiB).
.TP
.BI \-\-retention " MODE"
.B lossless
(default) keeps all input;
.B rolling
keeps only the most recent
.B \-\-memory\-budget
bytes of a stream, explicitly discarding older history.
.TP
.BI \-\-spool\-dir " DIR"
Directory for the private spool file (default: the system temporary directory).
.TP
.BI \-\-metadata\-budget " BYTES"
Row and line index bytes kept in memory (default 8 MiB).
.TP
.BI \-\-metadata\-quota " BYTES"
Maximum row and line index size (default 256 MiB).
.TP
.BI \-\-chunk\-size " BYTES"
Allocation unit for buffered input (default 64 KiB).
.SS Other
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
Read this configuration file instead of the default.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-config
Validate the configuration, including option names that startup would
ignore, print the file used, and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-completion " SHELL"
Print a completion script for
.BR bash ,
.BR zsh ,
.BR fish ,
or
.B powershell
and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a summary of the options and exit.
.SH KEYS
Press
.B g?\&
in
.B glimpse
for the bindings in effect, including configured ones.
The defaults are:
.TP 18
.BR j ", " Down " / " k ", " Up
Scroll one row.
.TP
.BR Ctrl\-F ", " PageDown ", " Space " / " Ctrl\-B ", " PageUp
Scroll one screen.
.TP
.BR Ctrl\-D " / " Ctrl\-U
Scroll half a screen.
.TP
.BR gg ", " Home " / " G ", " End
Go to the first / last line;
.IB N G
goes to line
.IR N .
.TP
.BR h ", " Left " / " l ", " Right
Scroll unwrapped lines horizontally.
.TP
.BR / " / " ?
Search forward / backward.
.TP
.BR n " / " N
Repeat the search in the same / opposite direction.
.TP
.B :
Enter a command.
.TP
.B F
Toggle following the end of the input.
.TP
.B w
Toggle line wrapping.
.TP
.B #
Toggle line numbers.
.TP
.B R
Toggle coloring
.BI # RRGGBB
codes.
.TP
.B =
Toggle the statusline (cmdheight \-1 and \-2).
.TP
.B g?
Show all bindings.
.TP
.B Esc
Cancel a pending key sequence or search.
.TP
.BR q ", " zq ", " Ctrl\-C
Quit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP 22
.BI : N
Go to line
.IR N .
.TP
.BR :top ", " :bottom
Go to the first or last line.
.TP
.BR :q ", " :quit
Quit.
.TP
.BI ":set " OPTION "\fR, \fP:set no\-" OPTION
Enable or disable
.BR smart\-case ,
.BR ignore\-case ,
.BR case\-sensitive ,
.BR incremental ,
.BR highlight ,
.BR wrap ,
.BR line\-numbers ,
or
.BR hex\-colors .
.TP
.BI ":set jump\-target=" N
Change the jump target.
.TP
.BI ":set spool\-quota=" BYTES
Raise the stream storage quota and resume reading.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings are read from
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/glimpse/glimpse.toml
(usually
.IR ~/.config/glimpse/glimpse.toml ).
Options override environment variables, which override the file.
Every setting can be given as an environment variable named
.B GLIMPSE_
followed by its key in upper case with dots and hyphens replaced by
underscores, for example
.B GLIMPSE_CMDHEIGHT=1
or
.BR GLIMPSE_STATUSLINE_STYLES_MODE_BG=red .
.PP
Top-level keys are
.BR cmdheight ,
.BR chunk\-size ,
.BR follow ,
.BR follow\-name ,
and
.B jump\-target
(a fraction must be written
.B 0.5
or
.B \(dq.5\(dq
in TOML).
Tables:
.TP
.B [display]
.BR wrap ,
.BR line\-numbers ,
.BR hex\-colors ,
.BR ambiguous\-width ;
.B [display.line\-number\-style]
.BR fg ,
.BR bg ;
.B [display.unprintable]
.B char
(one cell wide; default U+FFFD),
.BR fg ,
.BR bg .
.TP
.B [search]
.BR smart\-case ,
.BR ignore\-case ,
.BR case\-sensitive ,
.BR incremental ,
.BR highlight ;
.B [search.highlight\-style]
.BR fg ,
.BR bg .
.TP
.B [storage]
.BR memory\-budget ,
.BR spool\-quota ,
.BR metadata\-budget ,
.BR metadata\-quota ,
.BR retention ,
.BR spool\-dir .
.TP
.B [statusline]
.B left
and
.B right
section lists
.RB ( mode ,
.BR filename ,
.BR search\-results ,
.BR line\-numbers ),
.BR separator\-open ,
.BR separator\-close ,
.BR fg ,
.BR bg ;
.B [statusline.styles]
per-section
.BR "{ fg, bg }" .
.TP
.B [keybinds]
.IB action " = [" keys... ]
replaces all default keys of an action with one key sequence, e.g.
.BR "top = [\(dqg\(dq, \(dqg\(dq]" ;
an empty array disables it.
View actions:
quit, cancel, top, bottom, up, down, page\-up, page\-down, half\-page\-up,
half\-page\-down, follow, toggle\-status, search\-forward, search\-backward,
search\-next, search\-previous, command, toggle\-wrap, scroll\-left,
scroll\-right, toggle\-line\-numbers, toggle\-hex\-colors, help.
Prompt actions:
search\-accept, search\-cancel, search\-left, search\-right, search\-start,
search\-end, search\-word\-left, search\-word\-right, search\-backspace,
search\-delete, search\-delete\-word\-backward, search\-delete\-word\-forward,
search\-clear\-before, search\-clear\-after, search\-history\-previous,
search\-history\-next.
.PP
Colors are ANSI palette names such as
.BR red " or " bright\-blue ,
which follow the terminal theme, or
.B #RRGGBB
values.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MAN_PN
Default label for standard input, set by
.BR man (1).
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Location of the configuration directory.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Location of the search and command histories.
.TP
.B TMPDIR
Directory for spool and index temporary files.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/glimpse/glimpse.toml
Configuration.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/glimpse/
Search and command history.
.SH EXAMPLES
Use
.B glimpse
as the default pager, for man pages, and for git:
.PP
.RS
.nf
export PAGER=glimpse
export MANPAGER=glimpse
git config \-\-global core.pager glimpse
.fi
.RE
.PP
Follow a log through rotation, with line numbers:
.PP
.RS
.nf
glimpse \-\-follow \-\-follow\-name \-N /var/log/app.log
.fi
.RE
.PP
Watch an endless stream with bounded memory:
.PP
.RS
.nf
journalctl \-f | glimpse \-\-follow \-\-retention=rolling
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR less (1),
.BR man (1),
.BR tail (1)
